# d/dx log2(x) = 1 / (x * ln(2)).  The pinned Torch build has no dedicated
# ``aten::log2_backward`` schema: ATen derives the input gradient from the
# autograd formula ``grad / (self * 0.6931471805599453)``, which materialises
# the denominator in the tensor dtype and only then divides.  Both steps run in
# float32 opmath for fp16/bf16, so the fused kernel below reproduces them by
# rounding the product back to the input dtype before the division.  The
# rounding is observable: a half-precision product can move by 2**-11 relative,
# and skipping it shifts the quotient by up to one ulp of the dtype.
#
# Triton only accepts constexpr-instantiated module globals inside a kernel.
LN2 = tl.constexpr(0.6931471805599453)

# Streaming configuration: one element per lane, 1024 elements per program.
# Inputs at or below ``_SMALL_INPUT`` elements are launch-latency bound, so they
# keep the one-element-per-lane shape over four times as many programs (256
# elements, one warp) to occupy more SMs.
_BLOCK_SIZE = 1024
_NUM_WARPS = 4
_SMALL_BLOCK_SIZE = 256
_SMALL_NUM_WARPS = 1
_SMALL_INPUT = 8192


